for m,r in means.sort_values('mean',ascending=False).iterrows():screen_table+=m.replace('_',r'\_')+' & '+fmt(r['mean'])+r' $\pm$ '+fmt(r['std'])+' & '+(val(held.loc[m]) if m in held.index else '--')+r'\\'+'\n'
screen_table+=r'\bottomrule\end{tabular}\end{table}\FloatBarrier'+'\n'
scope=r'''\subsection{Published-comparator scope and unavailable uncertainty}
The literature comparison includes the directly compatible GDPa3 endpoints available from the published competition and Jiang study. Amini\,et\,al. supply a relevant industrial PLM study, and FLAb2 supplies broader heterogeneous-benchmark context, but neither is assigned an unreported GDPa3 score. The FLAb2 source cited here is a preprint~\citep{flab2}. TAP and the clinical antibody landscape inform representation design rather than supplying trained GDPa3 regression competitors~\citep{raybould2019tap,jain2017}. No exhaustive state-of-the-art ranking across incompatible datasets is claimed.

NR identifies a specific evidence limit: archived routing/hybrid points, the combined-format condition, composite precision, the disagreement correlation, and the stored tabular learner screen lack retained prediction or replicate records sufficient for interval reconstruction. Those entries remain point estimates. This is distinct from the fixed historical coefficient matrix and per-antibody plots, for which a sampling interval is not defined by the plotted quantity. The uncertainty-bearing panels use the conditional bootstrap or fold-refit definitions specified in Methods.
'''
